<title>BELGIUM: EU to reply to Italian milk plan before weekend.</title>
<headline>EU to reply to Italian milk plan before weekend.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission is still studying an Italian proposal over the payment of EU fines for producing too much milk, but expects to reply by the end of the week, a spokesman said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;We are still looking at it but expect to respond by the end of Friday,&quot; the Commission spokesman said.</p>
<p>Italian farmers are due to pay fines amounting to 190 million Ecus for exceeding their 1995/96 EU milk production quota of 9.9 million tonnes by some 400,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>Farmers wanted the government to pay the fines but this is not allowed under EU rules.</p>
<p>Prime Minister Romano Prodi proposed that farmers pay a first instalment of the fines immediately, leaving the rest until a commission of inquiry has finished work.</p>
<p>Italian farmers are against paying even a first tranche.</p>
</text>
